<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!-- Base application theme. -->
    <style name="AppTheme" parent="Theme.AppCompat.Light.DarkActionBar">
        <!-- Customize your theme here. -->
        <item name="colorPrimary">@color/colorPrimary</item>
        <item name="colorPrimaryDark">@color/colorPrimaryDark</item>
        <item name="colorAccent">@color/colorAccent</item>
    </style>

    <style name="AppTheme.NoActionBar" parent="Theme.AppCompat.DayNight.NoActionBar">
        <item name="windowActionBar">false</item>
        <item name="windowNoTitle">true</item>
        <item name="android:background">@null</item>
    </style>


    <!--
      THE LAUNCH SPLASH ON ANDROID 12 AND NEWER.

      `Theme.SplashScreen` is the androidx core-splashscreen backport, which is what
      Android 12+ actually reads. Two things here are load-bearing and neither is
      obvious:

      1. `windowSplashScreenBackground` is the cream the web splash in
         `src/index.html` uses, so the handoff from splash to app has no colour jump.
         The value lives in `@color/splashBackground`.

      2. `windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon` is the ART ONLY, not the full splash image.
         The system masks and scales whatever it is given to fit a fixed icon slot, so
         putting the full 2732x2732 splash here would crop it to a tiny square. The
         launcher icon foreground is the correct asset: already art-only on a
         transparent field, sized for exactly this.

      WHY `postSplashScreenTheme` MATTERS. Without it the app stays on
      Theme.SplashScreen after launch and the real theme never applies.

      WHY `android:background` IS STILL HERE. On Android 11 and below the system
      ignores the three attributes above entirely and shows `android:background` as a
      plain window background. `launchAutoHide: false` in capacitor.config.ts only
      governs the 12+ path; older devices still need this drawable. Both are needed,
      and both are the same cream, so there is no flash on either path.

      NOTE: a double hyphen is illegal inside an XML comment, which is why CSS custom
      property names are spelled out in words rather than written literally.

      The icon here is the launcher foreground, whose art already sits at the 66% safe
      zone (see brand-assets/splash/icon.png). It is deliberately NOT further inset: this
      attribute gets no inset of its own, so an extra one here would make the mark
      visibly smaller on the splash than on the home screen.

      See `brand-assets/splash/icon.png` and `brand-assets/splash/splash.png` for the source art.
    -->
    <style name="AppTheme.NoActionBarLaunch" parent="Theme.SplashScreen">
        <item name="android:background">@drawable/splash</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/splashBackground</item>
        <item name="windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground</item>
        <item name="postSplashScreenTheme">@style/AppTheme.NoActionBar</item>
    </style>
</resources>